-- title:
--   Linearising a tame finite-order automorphism of a crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $\hat{\mathcal O}$ be a commutative local ring and $\pi \in \hat{\mathcal O}$ a non-unit which is a non-zero-divisor, and suppose some power of the maximal ideal of $\hat{\mathcal O}$ is contained in the ideal $(\pi)$. Write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel` $\hat{\mathcal O}\,\pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\hat{\mathcal O}[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi$, assumed to be local and complete with respect to its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$; let $U\,\pi, V\,\pi \in R$ be the two distinguished elements, whose product is $\mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi$, the image of the constant $\pi$. Let $e$ be a natural number whose image in $\hat{\mathcal O}$ is a unit, let $\zeta, \zeta' \in \hat{\mathcal O}$ satisfy $\zeta\zeta' = 1$ and $\zeta^e = 1$, and let $\sigma$ be an $\hat{\mathcal O}$-algebra automorphism of $R$ whose $e$-fold iterate fixes every element, with $\sigma(U\,\pi) \equiv \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\zeta \cdot U\,\pi$ and $\sigma(V\,\pi) \equiv \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\zeta' \cdot V\,\pi$ modulo $\mathfrak m_R^2$. Then there is a unit $\gamma$ of $R$ with $\gamma - 1 \in \mathfrak m_R$ such that $\sigma(\gamma\, U\,\pi) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\zeta \cdot (\gamma\, U\,\pi)$ and $\sigma(\gamma^{-1} V\,\pi) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\zeta' \cdot (\gamma^{-1} V\,\pi)$.
--
--   This is the linearisation step for the local model $\hat{\mathcal O}[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ of a crossing point: an automorphism of order dividing an invertible $e$ that is only tangent to the diagonal action $\mathrm{diag}(\zeta,\zeta')$ becomes exactly diagonal after rescaling the two branch parameters by $\gamma$ and $\gamma^{-1}$, which again satisfy $(\gamma u)(\gamma^{-1}v) = \pi$. It is used in the analysis of fixed subrings and of divisibility in the crossing model, by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_algHom_range_eq_fixedPoints_apply_U_apply_V_of_tangent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_algHom_range_eq_fixedPoints_apply_U_apply_V_of_tangent) and [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.dvd_and_exists_eq_mul_pow_of_apply_eq_mul_pow_of_range_eq_fixedPoints`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.dvd_and_exists_eq_mul_pow_of_apply_eq_mul_pow_of_range_eq_fixedPoints).
